        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that there was one day a small number of them gathered together to sing and to dance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:2",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And now the priests of king Noah, being ashamed to return to the city of Nephi, yea, and also fearing that the people would slay them, therefore they durst not return to their wives and their children.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "Mosiah 19:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 192,
            "end": 200,
            "text": "Mosiah 25:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 19:21.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 19:21",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 19,
                    "end": 19,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 21,
                        "end": 21
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 25:12.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 25:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:3",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And having tarried in the wilderness, and having discovered the daughters of the Lamanites, they laid and watched them;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:4",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And when there were but few of them gathered together to dance, they came forth out of their secret places and took them and carried them into the wilderness; yea, twenty and four of the daughters of the Lamanites they carried into the wilderness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 196,
            "text": "Mosiah 21:20; 23:33 (30–35)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:5",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when the Lamanites found that their daughters had been missing, they were angry with the people of Limhi, for they thought it was the people of Limhi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:6",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore they sent their armies forth; yea, even the king himself went before his people; and they went up to the land of Nephi to destroy the people of Limhi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:7",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And now Limhi had discovered them from the tower, even all their preparations for war did he discover; therefore he gathered his people together, and laid wait for them in the fields and in the forests.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Mosiah 11:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 11:12.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 11:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:8",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when the Lamanites had come up, that the people of Limhi began to fall upon them from their waiting places, and began to slay them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:9",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the battle became exceedingly sore, for they fought like lions for their prey.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:10",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the people of Limhi began to drive the Lamanites before them; yet they were not half so numerous as the Lamanites. But they fought for their lives, and for their wives, and for their children; therefore they exerted themselves and like dragons did they fight.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 149,
            "end": 155,
            "text": "Alma 43:45."
          },
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 192,
            "text": "Alma 46:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 43:45.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 43:45",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 43,
                    "end": 43,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 45,
                        "end": 45
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Alma 46:12.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 46:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 46,
                    "end": 46,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:11",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that they found the king of the Lamanites among the number of their dead; yet he was not dead, having been wounded and left upon the ground, so speedy was the flight of his people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:12",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And they took him and bound up his wounds, and brought him before Limhi, and said: Behold, here is the king of the Lamanites; he having received a wound has fallen among their dead, and they have left him; and behold, we have brought him before you; and now let us slay him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:13",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But Limhi said unto them: Ye shall not slay him, but bring him hither that I may see him. And they brought him. And Limhi said unto him: What cause have ye to come up to war against my people? Behold, my people have not broken the oath that I made unto you; therefore, why should ye break the oath which ye made unto my people?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 231,
            "end": 235,
            "text": "Mosiah 19:26 (25–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:14",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And now the king said: I have broken the oath because thy people did carry away the daughters of my people; therefore, in my anger I did cause my people to come up to war against thy people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:15",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And now Limhi had heard nothing concerning this matter; therefore he said: I will search among my people and whosoever has done this thing shall perish. Therefore he caused a search to be made among his people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:16",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Now when Gideon had heard these things, he being the king’s captain, he went forth and said unto the king: I pray thee forbear, and do not search this people, and lay not this thing to their charge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Mosiah 19:23 (4–8, 23); 22:3; Alma 1:8 (8–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:17",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "For do ye not remember the priests of thy father, whom this people sought to destroy? And are they not in the wilderness? And are not they the ones who have stolen the daughters of the Lamanites?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:18",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, behold, and tell the king of these things, that he may tell his people that they may be pacified towards us; for behold they are already preparing to come against us; and behold also there are but few of us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:19",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, they come with their numerous hosts; and except the king doth pacify them towards us we must perish.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:20",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "For are not the words of Abinadi fulfilled, which he prophesied against us—and all this because we would not hearken unto the words of the Lord, and turn from our iniquities?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Mosiah 12:2 (1–8); 21:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 20:21",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And now let us pacify the king, and we fulfil the oath which we have made unto him; for it is better that we should be in bondage than that we should lose our lives; therefore, let us put a stop to the shedding of so much blood.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Mosiah 19:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 159,
            "end": 164,
            "text": "TG Life, Sanctity of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 19:26.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 19:26",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 19,
                    "end": 19,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 26,
                        "end": 26
                      }
                    ]
